# Chat Page Declutter & UX Optimization Plan

Goal: Make chat load feel instant (like a modern messenger) while cutting duplicate / non‑critical requests, reducing DB load, and preserving high‑quality AI context.

---

## 1. Core UX Intent

Critical at initial open:
- Last N (≈30) messages
- Character basic info (name, avatar, short description)
- Active persona (if set)
- Current context snapshot
- Enough settings to render composer (mode, memory toggles)

Non‑critical (lazy / deferred):
- Credits / plan
- World info full entries
- Memories & summaries
- Long history pagination
- Addon / feature metadata
- Embeddings / context expansion

---

## 2. Current Pain Points (From Request Flood)

| Issue | Impact |
|-------|--------|
| Duplicate recent messages fetches | Bandwidth & wasted latency |
| Separate queries for persona, character, settings, context | RTT fan‑out |
| Immediate refetch of context after creating/updating it | Redundant |
| Per‑chat message count queries | N+1 scaling |
| Early fetch of credits, memories, world info | Slower first paint |
| Over‑invalidation after send | Triggers storm of refetches |
| Parallel overlapping hydration logic in multiple hooks | Races & duplicates |
| Two message entry paths (recent vs pagination) | First page fetched twice |
| Summaries/memories fetched on every send | Unnecessary cost |
| Context extraction chains cause secondary GETs | Latency & clutter |

---

## 3. Target Load Sequence (T Timeline)

| Time | Data |
|------|------|
| T0 (blocking) | Hydration bundle (messages + character + persona + settings + context) |
| T+0–200ms (async) | Credits (only if composer needs gating) |
| T+0.2–1s | Memory summary meta, world info IDs |
| T+1–2s (idle) | Full world info details, memory expansions, summaries |
| On demand | Additional pages, analytics, embeddings |

---

## 4. Architectural Changes

1. Single edge function operation: `hydrate-chat`
2. New frontend hook: `useChatHydration(chatId, characterId)`
3. Derive all initial data slices from hydration cache (no extra queries)
4. Realtime subscriptions for:
   - `messages` (INSERT)
   - `chat_context` (UPDATE/INSERT)
5. Local cache patching instead of broad invalidations
6. Aggregated sidebar data via `chat_overview` RPC/materialized view
7. Memory & world info lazy expansion (interaction-triggered)
8. Throttle context extraction; avoid immediate fetch after persist

---

## 5. Backend Additions

### hydrate-chat (Edge Function)
Returns:
```
{
  chatId,
  recentMessages: Message[],
  character: { id, name, avatar_url, short_description },
  persona: { id, name, bio, lore } | null,
  settings: { character: {...}, global: {...} },
  context: existing chat_context row (or null),
  latestSummary: { id, message_count, created_at } | null,
  credits?: { balance, ... } (optional flag)
}
```

### chat_overview RPC / View
Single call returns for user:
```
[
  { chat_id, last_message, last_message_is_ai, last_message_at, message_count }
]
```
Used for sidebar without per-chat queries.

### Index & Schema Improvements
- `CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS messages_chat_order_idx ON messages(chat_id, message_order DESC);`
- `CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS chat_context_composite_idx ON chat_context(chat_id, user_id, character_id);`

