## 7. Query Strategy & Cache

| Data | Fetch | staleTime | Notes |
|------|-------|-----------|-------|
| Hydration | Single POST | 60s | Manual refresh on send if needed |
| Messages (new) | Realtime append | Infinite | No refetch unless pagination |
| Pagination pages | GET w/ cursor | 5m | No overlap with first page |
| Credits | Lazy (composer need) | 30s | Skip on pure read |
| Persona/Character | From hydration | 10m | Rarely change |
| Memories/Summaries | Lazy panel open | 5m | Not in initial path |
| World info | Metadata minimal first | 10m | Full on demand |

---

## 8. Invalidation Rules

| Event | Action |
|-------|--------|
| User sends message | Optimistic append to messages cache; no hydration refetch |
| AI streaming start | Insert placeholder; update progressively |
| AI streaming end | Finalize message; if context mutated, let realtime update context slice |
| Summary created | Invalidate summaries key only |
| Memory updated | Patch memory slice; do not refetch messages |
| Persona change | Invalidate hydration (single) and re-run hydration call |

---

## 9. Memory & Context Optimization

- Trigger memory fetch only if: enhancedMemory enabled AND (conversation length > threshold OR user input length > X).
- Introduce memory index endpoint: returns top candidate memory IDs + scores.
- Fetch full memory content only for top K (e.g., 5–8) before prompt assembly.
- Avoid re-querying full context after we already have it; just update via realtime.

